MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me felt like a natural next choice because Christmas music appears repeatedly in my listening history, and it is the one album I would try today.",
    "Home for Christmas, Christmas, and Noel also connect with that repeated holiday interest, even though that connection alone would not make me choose all of them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Partners, Cheek to Cheek, and To Be Loved give me no clear connection to the Christmas listening that made my chosen album appealing.",
    "The Lesley Gore and Merle Haggard collections do not connect to a specific interest in my recent choices, while The Very Best Of leaves me unsure whose music I would be choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to assume that an interest in a few albums means I also want a broad range of other singers and collections.",
    "A best-of collection is not appealing to me simply because it gathers an artist's familiar songs; I need a reason to want that artist."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas listening is a clearer reason for interest than a loose connection between albums, although those holiday interactions happened well before my latest choice.",
    "I rarely choose something unless it feels clearly relevant: several holiday albums can appeal to me while only one earns a selection, and artist identity still matters for titles such as Christmas."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my repeated interest in Christmas music but stretched that interest too far into unrelated singers and collections."
}
